  "acceptance": {
    "1": "Two labs/projects, independent/fixed/expiring shares and two retained releases are captured. Post-backup share/token revocation, membership removal, principal disablement and atomic stewardship transfer have independent durable acknowledgements and source-side authorization oracles.",
    "2": "Disposable original service, PostgreSQL catalog, object storage, import source, old package and local capture directory are removed. A UID-10005 reader downloads from a UID-10004 store. Fresh DB role/credentials and volumes are used; UID-10001 witness has no original source mounts or DB environment; protected witness trust is read only.",
    "3": "Independent exact catalog-row and full-export/metadata oracles pass. Old tokens, removed membership, disabled principal, expired share and former dataset-steward management are denied. Fresh legitimate reads and new-steward management succeed.",
    "4": "Exact metadata/content exports, protected receipt retries and fixed-release boundaries pass. Real revocation after the first 65536 delivery bytes refuses the next chunk. Old import/delivery tokens fail and pending work is reacquired. Missing dataset/release restrictions and ID-reuse denial survive.",
    "5": "Unavailable/stale/truncated/reordered/tampered witness, unsupported profile, corrupt/missing blobs and unresolved PREPARE refuse. Seven real process kills and new-writer-not-admitted retry keep recovery closed until the same session finishes. The separate O03.7 matrix observes a live stale writer.",
    "6": "Exact source/package/script/harness identities, observed UID/mount/network configuration, raw commands/outcomes, durable receipts and measured catalog/API/full-export times are retained. Zero acknowledged restrictions are lost. All retained backup-point science is exact; one later empty dataset and one later release are outside the scientific backup point and remain absent with restrictive tombstones."
  },
